    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0192" n="172" xml:id="pg172"/>

                <head>Mr. Dayton to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 559.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 8, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: You will doubtless have observed that M.
                    Galvez, the minister from Peru at this court, has been recently recalled and a
                    successor appointed to the post. At our last interview M. Drouyn de l’Huys
                    informed me that he had again recently communicated the views of France to Spain
                    urging peace between her and Peru. He says, furthermore, that Mr. Mercier, the
                    new ambassador to that court, will go out specially instructed to do what he can
                    in the interest of peace between those two countries. These things were
                    mentioned to me incidentally, and not, as it seemed to me, with any special view
                    to have them communicated by me to your department.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
